<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9771" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντηρίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>prop, stay, support,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1111
			</span></i>: pl., <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				8.4.6
			</span></i>; <i>stanchion</i> or <i>strut</i> in torsion-engines,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				<u>Bel.</u>
				76.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Bel.</u>
				101.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρκύων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyn.</u>
					10.7
				</span></i>
			; in <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.36
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντηρίδες</span> are <i>stay-beams</i>
			fixed inside a ship's bow, and projecting beyond it, so as to
			support and strengthen the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπωτίδες.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>=<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυρίς,</span>
			<i>window,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>:—and in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				785
			</span></i> it must mean <i>nostrils,</i> if it be the right reading.
				[<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐδος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i> ll.cc.: hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντήρειδες</span>
			in <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				<u>Poliorc.</u>
				178.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Bel.</u>
				101.9
			</span></i>, is wrong; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-είδιον</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				89.4
			</span></i> is 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίδιον</span>
			 as Inscrr. show.] (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ηρῐδ</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ερῐδ-</span>
			, weak form of stem of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρείδω</span>
			(cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρις</span>).)</div>
